# The agent image is built with `COPY nanoagent/ ./nanoagent/`, which takes the
# directory verbatim. .gitignore does NOT apply to a Docker build context, so
# anything ignored for git but present on disk still gets baked into the image
# unless it is listed here.

# Live credentials. agent/voice/.env holds real Gemini and Exotel keys during
# local development; without this line every built agent image carries them.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local databases — agent/voice/voice_agent.db holds real call records and
# transcripts, which are customer data and have no business in an image.
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
# ...but the vendored engine ships a READ-ONLY reference database of real WebGL
# vendor/renderer pairs, and it is not customer data. The blanket rule above stripped
# it from the build context, so COPY never saw it and the engine died at launch with
# "sqlite3.OperationalError: unable to open database file" — a packaging fix in
# pyproject.toml alone did not help, because the file was already gone before the
# wheel was built. Re-include it explicitly rather than narrowing the rule above:
# the secrets exclusion should stay blunt.
# NB the doubled prefix: the build context root is container/, and the package lives
# at container/nanoagent/nanoagent/... — a single "nanoagent/" here silently matches
# nothing, which is exactly how this was wrong on the first attempt.
!nanoagent/nanoagent/agent/effector/engine/webgl/webgl_data.db

# Call recordings and server logs (call audio).
**/logs/

# Build/test noise that only inflates the image.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.venv/
**/node_modules/
